  "summary": "Full assessment of all 763 French/Vietnamese passages: the Préface, three Placets, cast list and five acts, translated directly from the French Wikisource transcription. The first reviews of four ranges scored 8.23, 8.33, 8.53 and 7.78 and found seven majors (a garbled Pernelle line, an unintelligible ‘élancements’, Orgon calling Tartuffe ‘hắn’, a misidentified brother, an inverted ‘Taisez-vous’ line, a garbled argument and a mistranslated tirade); several further rounds of fixes and fresh separate-context blind reviews followed, with an attempt to force end-rhyme found to hurt the score and withdrawn. The final reviews scored 8.80, 8.80, 8.73 and 8.60 for the four ranges. Further majors found in the later reviews (units 472, 527 and 753) were fixed by hand without a further blind review of the whole range; the range with the lowest score, 8.60 on the half-point scale, sets the final score, equal to the unchanged 8.6 threshold. Open minors include occasional plain rather than rhymed verse, the Loyal pun in plain sense and a stiff intensifier.",
